Races a schema change against forming a statement's query plan.

The fingerprint code records a query plan per statement, built from the
table's index schemas.  It used to be formed after the statement ran, when a
socksql write has already released its table locks, so a rebuild finalizing
then freed the schemas being read.  The plan is now formed at prepare time,
under the schema lock.

Taking the schema lock after the statement ran is not an option: a read still
holds its table locks there, and finalize takes the schema lock before the
table lock, so the two deadlock.  The last scenario checks for that.

debug_sleep_in_cursor_description widens the window between picking the
index schema and reading it.  debug_sleep_before_fingerprint holds a statement
with its table locks between running and recording its fingerprint.
debug.poison_freed_schemas (COMDB2_TEST builds only) makes a read of a freed
schema crash instead of passing unnoticed.
